# User Profile API Cache Layer

**Simple in-memory cache:**

```javascript
class UserProfileCache {
  constructor(ttlMs = 5 * 60 * 1000) {
    this.cache = new Map();
    this.ttl = ttlMs;
  }

  get(userId) {
    const entry = this.cache.get(userId);
    if (!entry) return null;
    if (Date.now() > entry.expiresAt) {
      this.cache.delete(userId);
      return null;
    }
    return entry.data;
  }

  set(userId, data) {
    this.cache.set(userId, {
      data,
      expiresAt: Date.now() + this.ttl
    });
  }

  clear(userId) {
    this.cache.delete(userId);
  }
}

// Usage
const cache = new UserProfileCache(5 * 60 * 1000); // 5 min TTL

app.get('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const cached = cache.get(req.params.id);
  if (cached) return res.json(cached);

  const profile = await db.getUser(req.params.id);
  cache.set(req.params.id, profile);
  res.json(profile);
});
```

**Production (Redis):**

```javascript
const redis = require('redis');
const client = redis.createClient();

app.get('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  const key = `user:${req.params.id}`;

  let profile = await client.get(key);
  if (profile) return res.json(JSON.parse(profile));

  profile = await db.getUser(req.params.id);
  await client.setEx(key, 300, JSON.stringify(profile)); // 5 min TTL
  res.json(profile);
});

// Invalidate on profile update
app.patch('/api/users/:id', async (req, res) => {
  await db.updateUser(req.params.id, req.body);
  await client.del(`user:${req.params.id}`);
  res.sendStatus(204);
});
```

**Key decisions:**
- TTL prevents stale data; 5 min typical for profiles
- Invalidate cache on writes (not poll-based)
- Redis for distributed systems; in-memory for single instance
- Serialize JSON for Redis storage
